	"Name": "Witchy Valley",
	"Author": "sopholophagus",
	"Description": "[font=Tahoma][size=4]What it is:[/size]\n<br />\n<br />Witchy Valley allows you to learn and brew potions in a new cauldron crafting item.\n<br />\n<br />[size=4]How to Use:\n<br />\n<br />[/size]You will learn potion recipes from the wizard. The first letter will arrive in the mail after (early game spoiler) [spoiler]the wizard tells you about the Junimos at the Community Center[/spoiler] If you have already seen this event, the letter should have arrived when you load your save. \n<br />\n<br />To learn more potion recipes, you'll need to befriend the wizard. He will mail new recipes every 2 hearts. If you have already earned at least 2 hearts with the wizard, a new recipe will arrive once each day until you have learned all the unlocked recipes for your heart level.\n<br />\n<br />There is also an optional furniture pack that adds dried herbs, potion bottles, and decorative recipes! These can be purchased from Robin or generated from the furniture catalog.\n<br />\n<br />[size=4]Compatibility:\n<br />\n<br />[/size]SVE players will want to download Witchy Valley SVE, while normal players will want the normal Witchy Valley pack. The optional furniture pack is compatible with both vanilla Stardew and SVE.\u00A0\n<br />\n<br />For the optional furniture pack, those using the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/stardewvalley/mods/2276]Furniture Anywhere[/url] mod may need to download the Furniture Anywhere version of\u00A0[url=https://www.nexusmods.com/stardewvalley/mods/1254]Custom Furniture[/url]\uFEFF. This is untested with my mod and may not work.\n<br />\n<br />[size=4]Future Updates:\n<br />\n<br />[/size]I hope to continue to add more features to this mod, such as wands and more craftables. I'm open to ideas![/font]",
	"PageUrl": "https://www.nexusmods.com/stardewvalley/mods/7312",
